# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What Vercel must NOT upload. Same rule as vercel.json: Root Directory is set
# to portfolio_madebym, so this file belongs HERE, not at the repository root.
# At the repository root Vercel never reads it and the exclusions silently
# vanish — no error anywhere.
#
# Defence in depth, not the main gate. The main gate is .gitignore at the
# workspace root: Vercel deploys from Git, so a source file that is not in the
# repository can never reach this stage. This file catches the case where one
# gets committed by accident.
#
# Measured, not assumed — the three pages reference exactly 82 files, all of
# them under a *-web/ folder:
#     Slike/album-web/client-work      9
#     Slike/album-web/demo-projects   40
#     Slike/covers-web/client-work     9
#     Slike/covers-web/demo-projects   9
#     Slike/hero-web                  15
# Re-run this before editing the list below:
#     grep -ohE '(src|href)="Slike/[^"]*"' *.html | sort -u
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Poster sources — 231 MB against the 5 MB the site actually serves.
Slike/album/
Slike/covers/
Slike/hero/

# The six pre-redesign images, still tracked in Git but referenced by no page
# since "Selected work" was split into client-work.html and demo-projects.html.
# 15 MB of dead weight on every deploy. Excluding them is safe precisely
# because nothing links to them; deleting them is a separate decision.
Slike/*.png
Slike/*.jpg

# Hero mark derivatives, replaced by the live-text wordmark.
Slike/logo/logo-mark.png
Slike/logo/logo-mark.webp

# Internal documentation. Measured 2026-09-18: README.txt answered 200 at
# https://www.madebymstudio.com/README.txt — it is a public page today. It
# names the Formspree form ID, states that every anti-spam check runs in the
# browser and can be skipped, and flags that the real gate still has to be
# switched on in the dashboard. None of that belongs on a public URL.
README.txt

# Build inputs for tailwind.css, not assets the site needs. They stay in Git so
# the CSS can be regenerated, but there is no reason to serve them: measured
# 2026-09-20, tailwind.config.js answered 200 on the live domain.
tailwind.config.js
tailwind.input.css
